1
00:00:10,176 --> 00:00:11,219
Jane?

2
00:00:14,055 --> 00:00:15,223
Jane?

3
00:00:19,435 --> 00:00:21,354
- Good morning, Lisbon.
- Hi.

4
00:00:22,688 --> 00:00:25,358
- What happened to your wrist?
- Ah, it's nothing. I tripped.

5
00:00:25,525 --> 00:00:26,817
What are you doing?

6
00:00:28,945 --> 00:00:31,489
We're close. Very close.

7
00:00:31,948 --> 00:00:37,078
- How close is very close?
- Oh... about, uh, this close.

8
00:00:37,203 --> 00:00:39,830
- Tell me.
- No. First I need to sleep.

9
00:00:39,956 --> 00:00:43,084
- No, first you need to tell.
- I haven't slept in a week, Lisbon.

10
00:00:43,209 --> 00:00:44,293
- I am beat.
- Jane...

11
00:00:44,418 --> 00:00:45,670
I need to sleep.

12
00:00:45,795 --> 00:00:47,171
Come on. You're killing me!

13
00:00:47,296 --> 00:00:49,257
Just gonna take
a little rest here.

14
00:00:49,465 --> 00:00:51,634
Just a little one.
Just a little sleep.

15
00:00:51,759 --> 00:00:52,885
Jane.

16
00:01:15,491 --> 00:01:16,534
Okay.

17
00:01:17,535 --> 00:01:18,744
Thank you.

18
00:01:38,764 --> 00:01:39,849
Jane?

19
00:01:40,600 --> 00:01:41,684
Wake up.

20
00:01:41,809 --> 00:01:43,019
Jane. Come on.

21
00:01:53,487 --> 00:01:55,072
Where... what is it?

22
00:01:55,489 --> 00:01:58,784
We got a call on a homicide
in a motel in east Sac.

23
00:01:58,951 --> 00:02:00,328
Yeah?

24
00:02:00,911 --> 00:02:03,456
The first responders say
it looks like Red John.

25
00:02:31,776 --> 00:02:34,945
So what do you think?
Is this bogus, or actual Red John?

26
00:02:35,196 --> 00:02:38,491
I've worked Red John's murder scenes
since he began. It's totally bogus.

27
00:02:38,616 --> 00:02:40,117
Ah, that's a shame.

28
00:02:40,242 --> 00:02:42,370
I always wanted to work
one of the famous killers.

29
00:02:42,662 --> 00:02:46,374
Eh, he's been laying low for years
working through friends and proxies.

30
00:02:46,791 --> 00:02:49,960
- He killed just recently, didn't he?
- Eh, that was an internal issue.

31
00:02:50,086 --> 00:02:53,172
Lorelei Martins was one
of his own people. It doesn't count.

32
00:02:53,297 --> 00:02:55,132
Could you guys give us a moment?

33
00:02:55,299 --> 00:02:58,219
Hey, Lisbon.
Jane.

34
00:02:58,844 --> 00:03:02,056
- Uh, this is my colleague Val Ziskin.
- Hi.

35
00:03:02,181 --> 00:03:04,558
You're sure this wasn't Red John
are you, Mr. Partridge?

36
00:03:04,725 --> 00:03:07,311
- Uh... yeah.
- You 100% sure?

37
00:03:07,478 --> 00:03:10,606
No, I mean, I'm surmising.
You're the expert.

38
00:03:12,566 --> 00:03:14,360
Well, you heard
what she said.

39
00:03:14,694 --> 00:03:16,278
- Excuse me?
- Out.

40
00:03:16,445 --> 00:03:17,780
- I have a job to do.
- Out.

41
00:03:17,905 --> 00:03:19,407
You can come back later.

42
00:03:26,539 --> 00:03:27,998
Do you think he's right?

43
00:03:39,343 --> 00:03:42,096
- This is Red John.
- How can you tell?

44
00:03:42,388 --> 00:03:44,348
Because when it's him,
I can feel it.

45
00:03:46,600 --> 00:03:48,853
She looks familiar.
What do we know about her?

46
00:03:48,978 --> 00:03:51,897
She's a Jane Doe.
She's been at the motel for five days.

47
00:03:52,064 --> 00:03:54,316
Paid cash. Checked in
under a false name.

48
00:03:54,942 --> 00:03:57,153
As you can see,
she had a baby with her

49
00:03:57,278 --> 00:03:59,238
around 6 months old,
that went missing.

50
00:03:59,405 --> 00:04:01,031
Not Red John's M.O. at all.

51
00:04:01,157 --> 00:04:05,453
True. He must have had an accomplice
who needed a baby for some reason.

52
00:04:05,578 --> 00:04:07,538
Or it's not Red John.

53
00:04:15,629 --> 00:04:16,922
No, it's him.

54
00:04:28,225 --> 00:04:32,146
Uh, yes, hi. Uh...
Where are your offices located?

55
00:04:34,064 --> 00:04:35,149
Thank you.

56
00:04:37,526 --> 00:04:41,614
Child Protective Services.
Carson Springs.

57
00:04:42,531 --> 00:04:44,200
Well, you say that like it's bad.

58
00:04:44,325 --> 00:04:47,036
Yeah, well, when I was a kid,
I spent a little time there.

59
00:04:47,328 --> 00:04:48,996
You think it's connected?

60
00:04:50,122 --> 00:04:51,499
Probably not.

61
00:05:12,710 --> 00:05:16,463
It's strange. Right at this precise
moment when you get close

62
00:05:16,588 --> 00:05:19,174
Red John reappears
and murders somebody.

63
00:05:19,591 --> 00:05:21,593
It's got to be a coincidence, right?

64
00:05:21,802 --> 00:05:23,137
I hope so.

65
00:05:25,139 --> 00:05:26,932
- Are you gonna make me beg?
- For what?

66
00:05:27,099 --> 00:05:30,561
Come on, stop it!
How close are you exactly?

67
00:05:32,020 --> 00:05:33,772
{\an8}Assuming Lorelei's
telling the truth

68
00:05:33,981 --> 00:05:37,818
{\an8}Red John is one of 1,357 men
who I've shaken hands with

69
00:05:37,985 --> 00:05:39,862
{\an8}since my wife and daughter
were killed.

70
00:05:40,612 --> 00:05:43,031
{\an8}I've whittled that list down
to only those men

71
00:05:43,198 --> 00:05:46,660
{\an8}who could have possibly been
at all Red John murder sites.

72
00:05:46,869 --> 00:05:48,120
And how many is that?

73
00:05:49,079 --> 00:05:50,956
{\an8}I have a list of seven names.

74
00:05:52,249 --> 00:05:54,960
That's great. That's amazing.
Tell me the names.

75
00:05:57,713 --> 00:05:59,214
{\an8}I don't think that
that's a good idea.

76
00:05:59,339 --> 00:06:01,717
- What? Are you kidding?
- Please watch the road.

77
00:06:02,968 --> 00:06:04,219
Yes, sir, I'm the night clerk.

78
00:06:04,344 --> 00:06:06,346
I was here all night
listening to the radio.

79
00:06:06,513 --> 00:06:08,390
She was being murdered
50 feet away from me.

80
00:06:08,557 --> 00:06:10,058
I couldn't hear a thing.
It's creepy.

81
00:06:10,225 --> 00:06:12,436
Any unusual visitors that night,
or earlier in the day?

82
00:06:12,603 --> 00:06:15,856
{\an8}No. Yes! Well, not yesterday,
but the day before

83
00:06:16,023 --> 00:06:17,900
{\an8}a guy walks in,
he asks me if we have a woman

84
00:06:18,066 --> 00:06:20,944
{\an8}with a baby staying, so I say no
because he looked like trouble.

85
00:06:21,069 --> 00:06:22,112
{\an8}And what does trouble look like?

86
00:06:22,237 --> 00:06:24,656
{\an8}A big white dude.
Um, brown hair, beard.

87
00:06:24,823 --> 00:06:27,576
{\an8}Um, foreign accent.
I think Irish, it was.

88
00:06:27,701 --> 00:06:29,620
{\an8}But when I tell the poor lady
about him

89
00:06:29,745 --> 00:06:32,080
{\an8}she says to me, "thank you,"
like I did the right thing.

90
00:06:32,206 --> 00:06:33,540
Could you identify him
if you saw him again?

91
00:06:33,707 --> 00:06:34,750
Oh, yeah, absolutely.

92
00:06:34,875 --> 00:06:37,252
We need to talk to the maid
that found the body... Sandra Guzman?

93
00:06:37,377 --> 00:06:38,879
Oh, she went home.
She's not here.

94
00:06:39,004 --> 00:06:41,173
Didn't the local police tell her
she had to stay to talk with us?

95
00:06:41,340 --> 00:06:44,176
{\an8}Yeah, she was really upset,
you know... shivering.

96
00:06:44,301 --> 00:06:45,719
She had blood all over her.

97
00:06:45,844 --> 00:06:47,596
{\an8}She tells me
that she's freaking out

98
00:06:47,721 --> 00:06:50,098
{\an8}and she couldn't talk to nobody,
and she had to go home.

99
00:06:50,265 --> 00:06:51,433
She couldn't talk why?

100
00:06:51,558 --> 00:06:53,268
{\an8}I don't know.
She's a strange one, you know?

101
00:06:53,393 --> 00:06:56,939
{\an8}She's one of those with black
hair, rings, goth-like, you know?

102
00:06:57,064 --> 00:07:00,234
- You have an address for Sandra?
- Yeah. Uh, in the office, I think.

103
00:07:00,359 --> 00:07:02,653
{\an8}Yes. Um... I could show you.

104
00:07:05,572 --> 00:07:06,865
Well, why won't you tell me?

105
00:07:06,990 --> 00:07:09,660
{\an8}If I tell you why I won't tell you
then you'll get mad at me.

106
00:07:09,785 --> 00:07:11,453
I'm already mad at you.
Just tell me.

107
00:07:11,578 --> 00:07:14,414
{\an8}No, you're not mad, you're just vexed.
There is a difference.

108
00:07:20,671 --> 00:07:21,755
{\an8}Hello.

109
00:07:22,005 --> 00:07:25,217
We're with the CBI.
We need to talk to whoever's in charge.

110
00:07:25,342 --> 00:07:26,385
Yes, ma'am.

111
00:07:28,804 --> 00:07:32,182
{\an8}Miss Gottlieb, we have
an unidentified murder victim.

112
00:07:32,307 --> 00:07:34,643
{\an8}And your phone number
was written on her wall.

113
00:07:34,935 --> 00:07:38,230
{\an8}I'm gonna show you a photo of the woman
and see if you recognize her.

114
00:07:38,438 --> 00:07:42,025
{\an8}- She's dead, so it may be disturbing.
- Oh, my gosh. Okay.

115
00:07:43,151 --> 00:07:44,236
You know her.

116
00:07:44,361 --> 00:07:46,655
It's Eileen.
Eileen Turner.

117
00:07:47,865 --> 00:07:50,826
What about Caitlyn?
Is she... is Caitlyn safe?

118
00:07:50,951 --> 00:07:52,786
- Is that her baby?
- Yes. Where is she?

119
00:07:52,953 --> 00:07:53,996
{\an8}We don't know.

120
00:07:54,121 --> 00:07:55,622
{\an8}Whoever killed Eileen
may have taken her.

121
00:07:55,789 --> 00:07:57,791
- Oh, my God!
- Do you have any...

122
00:07:57,916 --> 00:08:00,878
the man you want is Roddy Turner
Eileen's husband.

123
00:08:01,086 --> 00:08:02,588
Do you think he's responsible?

124
00:08:02,754 --> 00:08:05,340
{\an8}He was abusive towards her.
Violent.

125
00:08:05,465 --> 00:08:07,134
{\an8}She left him a week ago.

126
00:08:07,759 --> 00:08:10,971
We were helping her get
a restraining order against him.

127
00:08:11,138 --> 00:08:15,726
{\an8}Um... here we are.
His address is 1204 Stoney Ridge.

128
00:08:15,851 --> 00:08:17,227
- Wait.
- That's about...

129
00:08:17,936 --> 00:08:19,271
I know where that is.

130
00:08:19,438 --> 00:08:20,939
Uh, thank you.

131
00:08:23,692 --> 00:08:24,985
Thank you for your help.

132
00:08:25,110 --> 00:08:27,571
{\an8}- We may be back.
- Of course. Anything I can do.

133
00:08:32,576 --> 00:08:33,619
{\an8}Jane?

134
00:08:34,620 --> 00:08:37,497
{\an8}Stoney Ridge is a traditional
carny layover.

135
00:08:37,789 --> 00:08:39,791
{\an8}In the winter, when we would
go to Carson Springs

136
00:08:39,917 --> 00:08:41,793
{\an8}it's where we'd stay...
Stoney Ridge.

137
00:08:41,919 --> 00:08:44,046
{\an8}I mean, it's practically
my hometown.

138
00:08:44,212 --> 00:08:46,506
{\an8}- Oh!
- Yeah. "Oh."

139
00:08:56,975 --> 00:08:58,685
It must be a coincidence.

140
00:08:59,811 --> 00:09:02,731
Or Red John is deliberately
bringing me home.

141
00:09:02,940 --> 00:09:04,775
How would he even know
about this place?

142
00:09:12,240 --> 00:09:14,242
Holy smokes! Patrick!

143
00:09:14,409 --> 00:09:16,620
Hey, Pete! It's Patrick Jane!

144
00:09:16,745 --> 00:09:17,871
Hey, Sam.

145
00:09:18,038 --> 00:09:20,332
Patty, me boy!
It's good to see you!

146
00:09:20,999 --> 00:09:23,418
- Yeah.
- What the hell are you doing here?

147
00:09:25,504 --> 00:09:27,798
I'm sorry. We don't
have a formal I.D.

148
00:09:27,923 --> 00:09:29,591
but we're pretty sure it's her.

149
00:09:29,716 --> 00:09:32,761
We found her this morning
at the Torchlite Motel in Sacramento.

150
00:09:32,928 --> 00:09:34,638
- Where's Caitlyn?
- She's missing.

151
00:09:34,763 --> 00:09:36,181
- Missing?
- Oh, my God.

152
00:09:36,306 --> 00:09:39,893
We and several other agencies
are doing everything we can to find her.

153
00:09:40,310 --> 00:09:42,062
Now what's your connection
to Eileen?

154
00:09:42,187 --> 00:09:44,064
She's married to my nephew
Roddy.

155
00:09:44,398 --> 00:09:46,775
They've been living with us
for a while in the Airstream.

156
00:09:46,900 --> 00:09:48,276
I don't recall a nephew.

157
00:09:48,402 --> 00:09:52,030
My sister's boy. Came over
from Ireland five years ago.

158
00:09:52,155 --> 00:09:54,825
He's a lead rigger. Puts up
the big wheels and the coasters.

159
00:09:54,950 --> 00:09:56,994
- He's a good lad.
- Uh, where's Roddy now?

160
00:09:57,119 --> 00:09:59,371
He's been out driving around
looking for Eileen and Caitlyn

161
00:09:59,538 --> 00:10:00,706
ever since they went.

162
00:10:00,872 --> 00:10:02,916
We need to talk to him.
Does he have a phone?

163
00:10:03,458 --> 00:10:04,543
No.

164
00:10:04,668 --> 00:10:06,545
Oh, come on, Pete.
It's me. We're...we're family.

165
00:10:06,670 --> 00:10:09,339
I mean, how long have the Janes
and the Turners been traveling together?

166
00:10:09,506 --> 00:10:12,968
A hundred years now, probably.
Roddy's got no phone.

167
00:10:13,176 --> 00:10:16,388
Okay. So Eileen left
a week ago, yes?

168
00:10:16,763 --> 00:10:18,223
- Yeah.
- Why?

169
00:10:18,348 --> 00:10:19,766
We don't know.

170
00:10:20,017 --> 00:10:22,394
They'd been having
a hard time financially.

171
00:10:22,561 --> 00:10:26,023
And they're both Leos. That can cause
arguments but nothing serious.

172
00:10:26,189 --> 00:10:29,443
Caityln's social worker had mentioned
abuse and violence.

173
00:10:29,609 --> 00:10:32,821
In a pig's eye!
Social workers, eh?

174
00:10:33,196 --> 00:10:35,741
Last month, Roddy and Eileen
had a bit of a go

175
00:10:35,866 --> 00:10:38,952
and the cops came and
they made a big deal of nothing

176
00:10:39,119 --> 00:10:42,539
and they called in child welfare.
It was a bunch of nonsense.

177
00:10:42,664 --> 00:10:46,752
Eileen and Roddy love each other
and they're great parents.

178
00:10:46,877 --> 00:10:48,587
What kind of car
was Roddy driving?

179
00:10:49,087 --> 00:10:52,466
Gee, I... I don't know.
I think he borrowed it from a friend.

180
00:10:52,591 --> 00:10:54,009
What's his friend's name?

181
00:10:55,052 --> 00:10:57,679
- I can't remember. Do you remember?
- Nope.

182
00:10:57,846 --> 00:11:01,683
Caitlyn's life is at stake here.
We need your cooperation.

183
00:11:01,850 --> 00:11:04,936
Roddy didn't kill Eileen,
so he hasn't got Caitlyn.

184
00:11:05,062 --> 00:11:07,939
- You had another name in mind.
- No name in mind.

185
00:11:08,148 --> 00:11:09,983
All right. Have it your way.

186
00:11:11,902 --> 00:11:13,695
Pete's calling Roddy right now.

187
00:11:13,820 --> 00:11:16,239
If Roddy's innocent,
which I think he is

188
00:11:16,364 --> 00:11:18,408
he'll feel compelled
to go to the crime scene.

189
00:11:18,533 --> 00:11:20,410
If he's innocent,
why not contact the police?

190
00:11:20,535 --> 00:11:23,497
Oh, 'cause no man in that family's
gonna willingly contact the police.

191
00:11:25,665 --> 00:11:26,875
Hey.

192
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:28,835
- "Hi, boss."
- Where are you?

193
00:11:28,960 --> 00:11:31,379
We're looking for Sandra Guzman
the motel maid that found the body.

194
00:11:31,546 --> 00:11:34,091
- She's playing hard to get.
- "Oh, take a break from that."

195
00:11:34,466 --> 00:11:36,927
Get to the motel as quick
as you can and stake it out.

196
00:11:37,052 --> 00:11:39,262
We think the victim's husband
might be headed over there.

197
00:11:39,387 --> 00:11:41,181
Tell him he's innocent.
We just need to talk to him.

198
00:11:41,306 --> 00:11:44,518
Uh, we don't know if he's involved
but bring him in. Be careful.

199
00:11:44,643 --> 00:11:45,769
Will do.

200
00:11:48,772 --> 00:11:51,483
What makes you so sure
Roddy Turner's innocent?

201
00:11:51,775 --> 00:11:53,360
Well, I'm not sure about
anything right now.

202
00:11:53,485 --> 00:11:55,070
Except that you won't tell me
the names on the list.

203
00:11:55,195 --> 00:11:56,238
You're sure of that.

204
00:11:56,363 --> 00:11:58,740
Yeah, well, I should tell you
why I'm not gonna tell you.

205
00:11:58,907 --> 00:12:00,992
Some of the names
are people that you know

206
00:12:01,118 --> 00:12:02,577
and you'll start acting
differently around them

207
00:12:02,744 --> 00:12:04,704
- and you may tip them off.
- What?! No, I won't!

208
00:12:04,830 --> 00:12:06,498
Well... Yes, you will.

209
00:12:06,623 --> 00:12:08,166
You can't help yourself.
I mean, no offense

210
00:12:08,333 --> 00:12:09,876
but you have no dishonesty in you.

211
00:12:10,001 --> 00:12:12,504
I have dishonesty in me.
I can put on a front.

212
00:12:13,130 --> 00:12:14,840
This is you putting on a front...

213
00:12:16,133 --> 00:12:19,970
- No, it's not. I can keep secrets.
- Oh, okay.

214
00:12:26,560 --> 00:12:28,103
I have secrets from you.

215
00:12:28,436 --> 00:12:32,899
- Secrets you cannot imagine.
- Right. Well, of course.

216
00:12:33,066 --> 00:12:34,401
How about I tell you
three things about you

217
00:12:34,526 --> 00:12:36,945
that you think are secrets
from me that I actually know?

218
00:12:37,070 --> 00:12:38,280
Then will you be convinced?

219
00:12:38,446 --> 00:12:40,657
- Sure. Go ahead.
- Okay.

220
00:12:40,824 --> 00:12:42,659
You know what? Wait.
Don't bother.

221
00:12:42,784 --> 00:12:45,162
I won't stoop to playing
your silly games.

222
00:12:45,287 --> 00:12:46,580
Wise call.

223
00:12:48,540 --> 00:12:50,792
- Are these people I know well?
- Very well.

224
00:12:50,917 --> 00:12:52,502
- J.J. LaRoche?
- No.

225
00:12:52,627 --> 00:12:55,755
- Ardiles?
- Interesting guess. No.

226
00:12:55,922 --> 00:12:57,799
Would you tell me if I guess right?

227
00:12:59,801 --> 00:13:02,012
- Nope.
- You're killing me.

228
00:13:07,392 --> 00:13:10,812
- So what's new with you?
- Nothing.

229
00:13:11,605 --> 00:13:13,607
Same old, same old, huh?

230
00:13:15,066 --> 00:13:16,735
Yeah, me, too, pretty much.

231
00:13:17,861 --> 00:13:20,030
- Except for one thing.
- Yeah, I know.

232
00:13:20,906 --> 00:13:22,741
You know?
You know what?

233
00:13:22,908 --> 00:13:24,910
You and Van Pelt
are having sex again.

234
00:13:25,869 --> 00:13:27,996
Yeah. Yes.

235
00:13:28,413 --> 00:13:33,418
I mean, I wouldn't call it that.
"Having sex." Kind of... clinical.

236
00:13:34,461 --> 00:13:38,173
- You're not having sex?
- No. Uh... yes, we are, of course.

237
00:13:38,465 --> 00:13:40,217
But it's more than that.

238
00:13:41,134 --> 00:13:44,846
- We're in love.
- Yeah? No kidding. Congratulations.

239
00:13:45,013 --> 00:13:47,265
How did you know? We were
keeping it on the way down low.

240
00:13:47,390 --> 00:13:48,558
Good job.

241
00:14:01,446 --> 00:14:02,489
Could I help you?

242
00:14:05,659 --> 00:14:07,494
Hey! CBI! Stop!

243
00:14:09,162 --> 00:14:10,330
Hey!

244
00:14:15,416 --> 00:14:18,002
- Where is she?
- Roddy, stop that right now!

245
00:14:18,169 --> 00:14:20,797
Put your hands on your head!
Do it now!

246
00:14:21,381 --> 00:14:22,882
I was just doing my job,
and this maniac

247
00:14:23,007 --> 00:14:24,968
comes in and attacks me!
I thought I was gonna die!

248
00:14:25,134 --> 00:14:26,886
- You're alive. Be quiet.
- Where are they?

249
00:14:27,011 --> 00:14:29,764
Sir, we understand your anger,
and we're sorry for your loss

250
00:14:29,931 --> 00:14:32,725
but we want to talk quietly someplace.
You need to come back to our office.

251
00:14:35,353 --> 00:14:36,688
When did she leave you?

252
00:14:43,653 --> 00:14:45,530
Roddy, you need to talk to us.

253
00:14:46,239 --> 00:14:47,490
If you didn't do this,
we need to know

254
00:14:47,615 --> 00:14:49,784
so we can find the man
responsible.

255
00:14:49,909 --> 00:14:51,452
And find your child.

256
00:14:52,203 --> 00:14:55,290
- "You want to help us find Caitlyn, right?"
- "Let me go."

257
00:14:56,082 --> 00:14:58,126
You assaulted a cop
and a CSI technician.

258
00:14:58,293 --> 00:15:00,878
- You're not going anywhere.
- I need to find me daughter.

259
00:15:02,463 --> 00:15:04,924
Please. Let me go.

260
00:15:06,801 --> 00:15:09,512
- He didn't do it.
- Hold on. Uh, if he did do it

261
00:15:09,679 --> 00:15:12,140
he did at as some sort of accomplice
to Red John, right?

262
00:15:12,265 --> 00:15:17,312
True. But Red John always offers his friends
something that they don't have.

263
00:15:17,687 --> 00:15:19,188
Why does Roddy need
Red John?

264
00:15:19,355 --> 00:15:21,065
I mean, what's his motive?
Where's his child?

265
00:15:21,190 --> 00:15:22,817
Good questions.

266
00:15:22,942 --> 00:15:25,653
Still, I get the distinct feeling
that he's hiding something.

267
00:15:25,778 --> 00:15:29,115
Me, too. Same thing Pete
and Samantha were hiding.

268
00:15:29,574 --> 00:15:31,367
Someone else they suspect.

269
00:15:31,534 --> 00:15:33,870
Which would suggest
a family dispute.

270
00:15:34,329 --> 00:15:35,830
Yes, it does.

271
00:15:36,622 --> 00:15:38,750
Who is Eileen's family?
Where's she from?

272
00:15:39,959 --> 00:15:44,172
- Family name is Barlow.
- Barlow?

273
00:15:44,380 --> 00:15:45,798
Yeah, she was born
in Modesto.

274
00:15:45,965 --> 00:15:49,302
Her parents were Kevin
and Suzanne Barlow.

275
00:15:49,427 --> 00:15:52,138
They were killed in a car accident
when she was 3 years old.

276
00:15:54,515 --> 00:15:57,685
- She's Leelee Barlow.
- You knew her?

277
00:15:57,852 --> 00:16:00,521
Well, after Eileen's parents
were killed...

278
00:16:01,230 --> 00:16:02,857
she was raised
by her Uncle Sean.

279
00:16:02,982 --> 00:16:04,817
He was very close with my father.

280
00:16:05,735 --> 00:16:08,738
Yeah, well, they fell out over
a business deal became enemies.

281
00:16:08,905 --> 00:16:14,035
But, uh, I haven't seen Eileen
or Sean for at least 30 years.

282
00:16:14,160 --> 00:16:17,455
You think that Eileen's murderer is maybe
connected to this Sean Barlow?

283
00:16:17,622 --> 00:16:20,208
Well, Pete thinks so. Otherwise
he would have told me who she was.

284
00:16:20,333 --> 00:16:21,667
What else?

285
00:16:22,710 --> 00:16:25,213
There was something about
remembering Eileen Barlow

286
00:16:25,338 --> 00:16:26,714
that freaked you out...
what is it?

287
00:16:26,839 --> 00:16:27,882
Oh, you're getting good, Lisbon.

288
00:16:28,007 --> 00:16:30,885
Don't patronize me.
Just tell me. What's the deal?

289
00:16:35,014 --> 00:16:37,266
You know how some certain
little random

290
00:16:37,433 --> 00:16:39,602
childhood memories
stick with you forever?

291
00:16:39,769 --> 00:16:43,272
You know, and oftentimes they're associated
with a piece of music or a song?

292
00:16:43,481 --> 00:16:47,110
Sure. You know that song about
the cake being left out in the rain?

293
00:16:47,819 --> 00:16:50,363
I always see my mother feeding pigeons.
I don't know why.

294
00:16:50,530 --> 00:16:52,865
Whenever I think of
happy times in my childhood

295
00:16:53,825 --> 00:16:55,410
I see a certain image.

296
00:16:55,576 --> 00:16:58,413
It's... it's a fourth of July picnic.

297
00:16:59,497 --> 00:17:01,999
"You know, I'm about 12 or so
and there's music playing."

298
00:17:02,166 --> 00:17:05,169
"There's a... a young girl laughing"

299
00:17:05,837 --> 00:17:08,923
as she's being lifted
into the air by her father.

300
00:17:09,090 --> 00:17:10,341
Eileen Barlow.

301
00:17:10,508 --> 00:17:12,385
Well, people called her
Leelee back then.

302
00:17:14,470 --> 00:17:16,722
I don't think I ever
saw her again after that day.

303
00:17:18,724 --> 00:17:20,852
She's just a memory
that made me smile.

304
00:17:23,771 --> 00:17:25,148
And Red John killed her.

305
00:17:28,651 --> 00:17:32,989
I... It's like he just reached into my head
and killed a happy memory.

306
00:17:45,084 --> 00:17:46,961
How is it possible?

307
00:17:47,086 --> 00:17:49,964
- How could he read your mind?
- I don't know.

308
00:17:53,384 --> 00:17:58,055
- Hell of a trick, though, right?
- It's a coincidence. It must be.

309
00:17:58,639 --> 00:18:00,516
Yeah. Yeah, it must be.

310
00:18:01,058 --> 00:18:04,604
Uh, could you do me a favor?
Could wait in the car when I talk to Pete?

311
00:18:05,062 --> 00:18:06,898
- Okay.
- It's not that he dislikes you.

312
00:18:07,064 --> 00:18:10,359
It's just, you know, you're...
you're police.

313
00:18:11,861 --> 00:18:14,489
- I understand.
- Thank you.

314
00:18:18,576 --> 00:18:20,244
- What?
- You know what.

315
00:18:21,204 --> 00:18:22,580
So you say.

316
00:18:22,788 --> 00:18:24,916
Why didn't you tell me
Eileen was a Barlow?

317
00:18:25,041 --> 00:18:26,167
You didn't ask me.

318
00:18:26,292 --> 00:18:28,503
You think Sean Barlow
was behind her murder.

319
00:18:29,378 --> 00:18:30,963
And you're as calm
as you are about Caitlyn

320
00:18:31,130 --> 00:18:33,674
because you assume the Barlows
are gonna take good care of her.

321
00:18:33,799 --> 00:18:34,967
Is that so?

322
00:18:35,092 --> 00:18:37,845
And you're just waiting for me
and the cops to move on

323
00:18:37,970 --> 00:18:40,473
then you and Roddy are gonna
take care of this yourselves.

324
00:18:40,848 --> 00:18:41,891
No.

325
00:18:42,975 --> 00:18:46,938
The only thing
I don't know is why.

326
00:18:47,063 --> 00:18:50,399
Why would you think that Sean Barlow
would kill his own niece?

327
00:18:50,942 --> 00:18:54,570
- It's your theory, not mine.
- No. It's yours.

328
00:18:55,279 --> 00:18:58,282
And you're probably wrong.
This murder was done by Red John.

329
00:18:58,699 --> 00:19:00,952
I mean, Sean Barlow
may have helped him...

330
00:19:02,245 --> 00:19:05,915
But if he did, and you know he did
you better tell me why right now.

331
00:19:06,082 --> 00:19:09,085
- Like I said...
- Don't you even try to lie to me.

332
00:19:14,382 --> 00:19:17,260
Sean Barlow has always
hated Roddy.

333
00:19:17,426 --> 00:19:20,721
He forbade Eileen to see him,
but she did anyhow.

334
00:19:20,846 --> 00:19:24,350
- Why does he hate Roddy?
- The travel circuit

335
00:19:24,559 --> 00:19:27,812
in Britain and Ireland
is a tough go.

336
00:19:28,062 --> 00:19:30,398
And Roddy used to be
a little salty.

337
00:19:30,606 --> 00:19:33,276
Used to be.
He's a calmer fellow now.

338
00:19:33,943 --> 00:19:36,737
But he broke some faces
he should have left alone.

339
00:19:37,697 --> 00:19:41,284
He was one step ahead of trouble
when my sister sent him over here to me.

340
00:19:42,243 --> 00:19:47,498
Anyhow, some of the injured parties
were cousins to the Barlows

341
00:19:48,291 --> 00:19:51,961
and Sean Barlow loves
to cultivate a grudge.

342
00:19:52,128 --> 00:19:54,130
Grudge enough to murder
his own niece?

343
00:19:54,255 --> 00:19:56,090
You don't know Sean Barlow.

344
00:19:58,843 --> 00:20:02,305
He disowned Eileen,
called her a whore.

345
00:20:02,471 --> 00:20:07,226
He demanded money from Roddy
for payment for lost Barlow property.

346
00:20:08,227 --> 00:20:10,021
Roddy refused, of course

347
00:20:10,271 --> 00:20:14,150
and Sean accused him of theft
and swore vengeance.

348
00:20:15,901 --> 00:20:19,530
- Swore vengeance?
- In a manner of words, yeah.

349
00:20:19,822 --> 00:20:24,035
And what's his connection to Red John?
It doesn't quite fit.

350
00:20:24,160 --> 00:20:28,331
Sean Barlow is a sinister
piece of work.

351
00:20:28,956 --> 00:20:32,418
He's mean and clever.
Hell, Patty...

352
00:20:33,419 --> 00:20:37,465
For all I know, Sean Barlow
may be Red John.

353
00:20:40,426 --> 00:20:41,761
Give me an address.

354
00:21:06,827 --> 00:21:09,163
You know, you should
probably wait here.

355
00:21:09,288 --> 00:21:10,748
Not a chance in hell.

356
00:21:10,915 --> 00:21:13,584
Uh, he's old school like Pete.
He's not gonna want to talk to a cop.

357
00:21:13,751 --> 00:21:15,252
We'll see.
I'm old school, too.

358
00:21:15,419 --> 00:21:17,046
- Seriously.
- Seriously!

359
00:21:17,171 --> 00:21:20,299
I didn't come here all the way
from Sacramento to wait outside.

360
00:21:38,834 --> 00:21:41,920
Welcome, welcome.
You're very welcome.

361
00:21:42,027 --> 00:21:44,196
I'm Marta.
How can I help you?

362
00:21:44,363 --> 00:21:45,989
Relax, sister,
we're not chumps.

363
00:21:46,156 --> 00:21:48,117
She's a cop,
and I'm in on the gag.

364
00:21:48,325 --> 00:21:51,203
- What do you want?
- To talk to Sean Barlow.

365
00:21:51,370 --> 00:21:53,122
There's no Sean Barlow here.

366
00:21:53,288 --> 00:21:55,082
She's almost as bad
a liar as you are.

367
00:21:55,207 --> 00:21:57,376
You tell Sean...
who isn't here...

368
00:21:57,501 --> 00:22:00,963
that Patrick Jane is here,
and he'd like to talk to him. We'll wait.

369
00:22:08,262 --> 00:22:12,141
Patrick Jane. It is you.
I didn't believe her!

370
00:22:12,266 --> 00:22:13,475
Hello, Mr. Barlow.

371
00:22:13,600 --> 00:22:16,854
Oh... Call me Sean,
my boy...Sean.

372
00:22:16,979 --> 00:22:19,732
Well, I haven't seen you
since you were, what? 15?

373
00:22:20,399 --> 00:22:21,775
You haven't changed a bit.

374
00:22:21,942 --> 00:22:23,944
And you've brought
a policewoman with you.

375
00:22:24,111 --> 00:22:25,988
Great pleasure to meet you,
young lady.

376
00:22:26,405 --> 00:22:28,198
Come on upstairs
and let's catch up.

377
00:22:28,949 --> 00:22:31,243
I've been following
your doings, Patrick.

378
00:22:31,493 --> 00:22:34,204
- I know why you're here.
- Well, of course you do.

379
00:22:36,915 --> 00:22:41,420
My grandfather came over from Ireland
with this one's great grandfather.

380
00:22:41,670 --> 00:22:43,338
His father and I
were great friends.

381
00:22:43,464 --> 00:22:46,258
He was a wicked man,
but I loved him.

382
00:22:46,425 --> 00:22:48,093
A wicked man?

383
00:22:48,385 --> 00:22:50,304
You're a spiritual person,
aren't you, Teresa?

384
00:22:50,429 --> 00:22:52,139
- You believe in life after death?
- Yes.

385
00:22:52,306 --> 00:22:55,434
Then you'll agree it's a sad thing
to be an unbeliever

386
00:22:55,601 --> 00:22:57,686
- to have no faith.
- Yes.

387
00:22:57,811 --> 00:23:02,107
And when faithless men
use the faith and belief of others

388
00:23:02,274 --> 00:23:05,694
to steal from them with lies
like the Janes do.

389
00:23:05,861 --> 00:23:07,404
That's sad and wicked.

390
00:23:07,529 --> 00:23:10,324
I agree.
I don't do it anymore.

391
00:23:10,491 --> 00:23:12,785
No. A lawman now.

392
00:23:13,619 --> 00:23:15,579
It's atonement you're after, is it?

393
00:23:15,746 --> 00:23:18,040
Well, the Janes never
pretended to have powers

394
00:23:18,165 --> 00:23:19,500
especially with people
in the show

395
00:23:19,666 --> 00:23:26,048
but, the Barlows always tried to pass
themselves off as "real" psychics.

396
00:23:26,673 --> 00:23:28,091
Because we are.

397
00:23:28,258 --> 00:23:30,636
Well, you said you knew
why we were here.

398
00:23:31,762 --> 00:23:34,932
Yeah, it was on the news.
Eileen is dead, murdered.

399
00:23:35,098 --> 00:23:37,810
- You don't seem so upset about it.
- She was already dead to me

400
00:23:37,935 --> 00:23:40,395
when she left the family
for that scum.

401
00:23:40,687 --> 00:23:44,608
I mourned her passing long ago.
I want the baby, though.

402
00:23:44,775 --> 00:23:46,610
She'll be raised a Barlow.

403
00:23:46,735 --> 00:23:48,403
Where were you the night
before last?

404
00:23:48,570 --> 00:23:51,490
Oh, I was far away,
communing with the spirits.

405
00:23:51,657 --> 00:23:52,908
Where were you?

406
00:23:53,784 --> 00:23:55,035
Let me see.

407
00:23:58,247 --> 00:24:00,791
Lying in bed,
thinking of Patrick.

408
00:24:00,958 --> 00:24:03,043
You're a little in love
with him, eh?

409
00:24:03,210 --> 00:24:06,171
But he's so secretive
and controlling.

410
00:24:06,421 --> 00:24:08,131
That's hard, isn't it?

411
00:24:09,508 --> 00:24:11,385
We're here because of Eileen.

412
00:24:11,552 --> 00:24:14,847
It was that scum Roddy Turner
killed her, no doubt.

413
00:24:15,013 --> 00:24:16,974
Well, Roddy and his Uncle
say it was you.

414
00:24:18,016 --> 00:24:19,518
Words are cheap.

415
00:24:19,643 --> 00:24:22,145
It was Roddy she was afraid of,
wasn't it?

416
00:24:22,729 --> 00:24:25,023
It was him,
and God knows he'll pay.

417
00:24:25,148 --> 00:24:29,361
Well, whoever killed Eileen and took Caitlyn
they had help from Red John

418
00:24:29,486 --> 00:24:31,864
and you're more
the Red John type of man.

419
00:24:32,406 --> 00:24:36,118
Red John. Any punk killer
who wants to fool with you

420
00:24:36,285 --> 00:24:38,287
can paint a smiley face
on the wall.

421
00:24:38,495 --> 00:24:41,748
- "Oh, it's Red John"
- it was Red John.

422
00:24:42,165 --> 00:24:44,543
Red John has
your mind completely messed up.

423
00:24:44,668 --> 00:24:47,379
You see him every place
you look.

424
00:24:47,546 --> 00:24:50,549
You think you're getting closer,
but he is just playing with you.

425
00:24:50,674 --> 00:24:53,093
- We'll see.
- Has it never occurred to you

426
00:24:53,218 --> 00:24:56,597
to ask exactly how Red John
is always one step ahead of you?

427
00:24:57,139 --> 00:24:59,016
How is it he seems
to read your mind?

428
00:24:59,182 --> 00:25:01,310
- You tell me.
- Red John's got powers.

429
00:25:01,894 --> 00:25:05,147
Real psychic powers
that you refuse to believe in.

430
00:25:05,272 --> 00:25:08,609
Teresa will hear what I'm saying
but you've no faith

431
00:25:08,775 --> 00:25:10,652
so you're deaf to the truth.

432
00:25:10,861 --> 00:25:14,489
He's got powers.
That's why he'll always defeat you.

433
00:25:15,157 --> 00:25:18,035
So I take it you have no alibi
for the night before last.

434
00:25:18,160 --> 00:25:21,079
No. No, I don't.

435
00:25:21,330 --> 00:25:26,251
- Thank you for your time, Mr. Barlow.
- Entirely my pleasure.

436
00:25:26,460 --> 00:25:29,129
It's odd, isn't it
how the daughters of alcoholics

437
00:25:29,254 --> 00:25:31,840
so often are the best
kind of women.

438
00:25:33,800 --> 00:25:36,678
When you find the baby, bring her to me.
She'll be well looked after.

439
00:25:36,845 --> 00:25:38,263
That's not the way it works.

440
00:25:38,388 --> 00:25:41,767
Oh, does it not?
I'm sure we'll sort something out.

441
00:25:43,894 --> 00:25:45,479
Think on what I said.

442
00:25:45,771 --> 00:25:47,940
It's honest advice
from a friend.

443
00:25:48,649 --> 00:25:50,275
Good seeing you, Sean.

444
00:25:52,444 --> 00:25:56,740
Wow. That was intense.
You okay?

445
00:25:56,907 --> 00:25:59,743
Oh, I'm fine. You okay?
He didn't spook you, did he?

446
00:25:59,868 --> 00:26:01,453
Yeah. He didn't spook you?

447
00:26:01,578 --> 00:26:03,789
Ah, he's a good showman.
I'll give him that.

448
00:26:05,248 --> 00:26:06,625
I couldn't read him.

449
00:26:07,292 --> 00:26:10,504
He might have killed Eileen,
or... he might be right.

450
00:26:10,629 --> 00:26:12,589
Maybe he believes
that Roddy did do it.

451
00:26:13,799 --> 00:26:18,720
Or... Maybe I've just fallen
for some punk playing a trick.

452
00:26:19,179 --> 00:26:20,222
What if he's right?

453
00:26:20,347 --> 00:26:22,474
What if Red John really
does have powers?

454
00:26:22,683 --> 00:26:25,936
Please! And what if dolphins
were actually aliens

455
00:26:26,061 --> 00:26:28,021
from another galaxy?
That would be kind of cool.

456
00:26:28,188 --> 00:26:30,440
I'm serious. How did
Red John do what he did?

457
00:26:30,565 --> 00:26:31,775
He read your mind.

458
00:26:31,900 --> 00:26:34,027
It was a cool trick,
just like I said.

459
00:26:40,867 --> 00:26:42,744
We're looking for this woman...
Sandra Guzman... have you seen her?

460
00:26:42,869 --> 00:26:44,496
She just got on the bus.

461
00:27:28,540 --> 00:27:29,583
CBI!

462
00:27:36,131 --> 00:27:37,299
Hey, Sandra.

463
00:27:38,717 --> 00:27:40,343
Why have you been running
from us, Sandra?

464
00:27:42,387 --> 00:27:44,598
We just wanted to talk to you
about what you saw at the motel.

465
00:27:44,765 --> 00:27:48,101
Did you see in that room?
That was the devil in there.

466
00:27:48,226 --> 00:27:50,520
I don't want nothing to do with that.
I don't wanna talk about it.

467
00:27:50,645 --> 00:27:52,481
"I just want to forget
I ever saw it."

468
00:27:53,732 --> 00:27:56,902
- And how's that working out for you?
- Not so good.

469
00:27:57,069 --> 00:27:58,653
I can't sleep.

470
00:27:58,862 --> 00:28:02,449
Every time I close my eyes,
I see that poor woman.

471
00:28:02,699 --> 00:28:04,284
So maybe you do need
to talk about it.

472
00:28:05,952 --> 00:28:08,038
Tell me exactly what you saw
when you walked into the room.

473
00:28:09,331 --> 00:28:10,415
I was...

474
00:28:11,500 --> 00:28:16,004
I was pulling my cart in
so I didn't see the bed right away.

475
00:28:16,171 --> 00:28:20,509
And I was thinking she moved out
because before, when I did the room

476
00:28:20,675 --> 00:28:23,553
she had, like, stacks
of diapers and baby milk.

477
00:28:23,720 --> 00:28:25,472
But it was all gone.

478
00:28:25,680 --> 00:28:29,017
So I thought they left.
And then I turn around

479
00:28:29,684 --> 00:28:32,437
looked at the bed,
and, oh, my God.

480
00:28:33,021 --> 00:28:36,900
Her eyes were open,
looking right at me.

481
00:28:38,235 --> 00:28:40,195
I fell down,
I was so scared.

482
00:28:42,405 --> 00:28:45,408
The carpet was all wet
with her blood.

483
00:28:47,953 --> 00:28:49,579
And when you arrived
for work that morning

484
00:28:49,746 --> 00:28:51,873
did you notice any strangers?
Anybody acting weird?

485
00:28:52,040 --> 00:28:54,876
- Anything out of the ordinary?
- Nothing.

486
00:28:58,964 --> 00:29:03,802
- What happened to the baby?
- We don't know yet.

487
00:29:07,889 --> 00:29:09,683
The motel maid... blameless.

488
00:29:09,850 --> 00:29:11,893
But illuminating. We need
to go back to Carson Springs

489
00:29:12,060 --> 00:29:14,813
but first, you need to let
Roddy Turner go.

490
00:29:15,021 --> 00:29:16,314
Okay.

491
00:29:17,524 --> 00:29:18,733
Thank you.

492
00:29:19,317 --> 00:29:21,319
Okay, so we have
two prime suspects.

493
00:29:21,444 --> 00:29:24,865
Roddy Turner... Eileen's husband...
and Sean Barlow... her uncle.

494
00:29:24,990 --> 00:29:26,992
Both men are pointing at each
other as the guilty party.

495
00:29:27,117 --> 00:29:30,745
We need your help to find out
which one is in fact the killer.

496
00:29:31,204 --> 00:29:33,957
Uh, don't worry.
There'll be no danger.

497
00:29:34,124 --> 00:29:36,626
Oh, I don't mind that.
What's the plan exactly?

498
00:29:36,751 --> 00:29:38,795
We're gonna let both men know
that there is a baby...

499
00:29:38,920 --> 00:29:41,965
a baby that resembles baby Caitlyn...
that has been left here with you.

500
00:29:42,090 --> 00:29:44,843
Now we're assuming that
the killer has baby Caitlyn

501
00:29:45,010 --> 00:29:46,678
or knows where she is,
so he will know

502
00:29:46,845 --> 00:29:49,097
that the baby that's left here
with you is not her.

503
00:29:49,222 --> 00:29:52,184
Oh, I see.
So only the innocent man

504
00:29:52,309 --> 00:29:54,186
will show up to see
if the baby is Caitlyn.

505
00:29:54,352 --> 00:29:57,981
Exactly. And the guilty man
simply won't show.

506
00:29:58,231 --> 00:29:59,441
- Clever.
- If you're willing.

507
00:29:59,566 --> 00:30:00,942
- Of course.
- Splendid.

508
00:30:01,735 --> 00:30:02,819
Great.

509
00:30:02,944 --> 00:30:05,989
A little girl has been left
at the CPS offices in Carson Springs.

510
00:30:06,114 --> 00:30:08,283
I am trying to confirm I.D.
as Caitlyn Turner

511
00:30:08,491 --> 00:30:10,493
and you're listed
as one of the contacts.

512
00:30:10,619 --> 00:30:13,163
"Does Caitlyn have a small
birthmark on her left arm?"

513
00:30:13,330 --> 00:30:15,248
Yes. Yes, she does.

514
00:30:16,541 --> 00:30:18,210
- Yeah, hello?
- Hey, Sean.

515
00:30:18,627 --> 00:30:20,795
Some lady here says
they found baby Caitlyn.

516
00:30:26,718 --> 00:30:28,428
- Look...
- You know, I've been thinking.

517
00:30:28,678 --> 00:30:31,139
- So have I.
- You first.

518
00:30:32,515 --> 00:30:35,518
- I can't work like this...
- No, sorry, wrong. Me first.

519
00:30:35,769 --> 00:30:40,065
Sean was right. I've been...
secretive and controlling, and...

520
00:30:41,942 --> 00:30:43,818
I'm gonna tell you
the seven names on the list

521
00:30:43,985 --> 00:30:46,363
but you need to promise me
you will not tell

522
00:30:46,529 --> 00:30:49,199
another living soul... nobody.

523
00:30:49,366 --> 00:30:50,909
Well, how can I put them
under surveillance

524
00:30:51,076 --> 00:30:54,371
and investigate them if I can't tell
anybody at the CBI who they are?

525
00:30:54,496 --> 00:30:55,538
You can't.

526
00:30:55,664 --> 00:30:58,583
- But I don't have...
- Nobody. Especially the CBI.

527
00:30:58,708 --> 00:30:59,918
Why?

528
00:31:00,919 --> 00:31:04,464
Because one of the names
on the list is Gale Bertram.

529
00:31:04,631 --> 00:31:05,799
- What?
- Your boss.

530
00:31:05,924 --> 00:31:07,259
- No.
- Yes.

531
00:31:08,343 --> 00:31:11,763
Oh, my God.
How am I gonna face him?

532
00:31:12,055 --> 00:31:13,974
- Well...
- Who else?

533
00:31:15,100 --> 00:31:16,434
- Roddy Turner.
- What?

534
00:31:16,559 --> 00:31:17,602
Over there.

535
00:31:23,775 --> 00:31:25,443
Aye. They said you have
my daughter here.

536
00:31:25,568 --> 00:31:26,611
Mr. Turner?

537
00:31:26,736 --> 00:31:28,029
- Where's Caitlyn?!
- Mr. Turner!

538
00:31:29,698 --> 00:31:32,701
- What is this?
- I'm sorry. It was a false alarm.

539
00:31:32,867 --> 00:31:34,619
- Caitlyn's not here.
- What?

540
00:31:34,786 --> 00:31:37,080
It was a trick to flush out
Eileen's killer

541
00:31:37,539 --> 00:31:40,959
who didn't come because he knows
that Caitlyn wouldn't be here.

542
00:31:41,876 --> 00:31:43,712
This is interesting.

543
00:31:43,837 --> 00:31:45,880
Well, what the hell
is this then?

544
00:31:46,006 --> 00:31:47,590
Yes. Sorry.

545
00:31:47,757 --> 00:31:49,843
Sorry for what?
Where's Caitlyn?

546
00:31:50,010 --> 00:31:52,345
You know Roddy, don't you?

547
00:31:52,470 --> 00:31:55,974
Good news is you're both here,
which means neither of you killed Eileen.

548
00:31:56,099 --> 00:31:58,351
That's off to a reasonably
good start.

549
00:31:58,476 --> 00:32:00,312
Gentlemen, please don't
even think about it.

550
00:32:00,437 --> 00:32:02,939
Eileen would want you two
to be making peace.

551
00:32:03,064 --> 00:32:04,232
Like hell she would.

552
00:32:04,399 --> 00:32:08,528
- You had better have a damn good...
- Hold that thought.

553
00:32:09,946 --> 00:32:11,281
Excuse me.

554
00:32:11,448 --> 00:32:13,241
Uh, yes, Van Pelt?
You'd better talk very quickly.

555
00:32:13,408 --> 00:32:15,785
My phone is about to run out of juice
and I'm under a little pressure here.

556
00:32:15,952 --> 00:32:20,248
Hi. I'm calling like you said.
And good luck. I hope it works.

557
00:32:21,124 --> 00:32:24,461
What? Where?

558
00:32:25,295 --> 00:32:27,756
Uh, are you sure?
Yeah.

559
00:32:28,131 --> 00:32:30,342
Yeah, okay. We'll be right there.

560
00:32:31,426 --> 00:32:33,053
Wow, you're not gonna
believe this.

561
00:32:34,095 --> 00:32:37,307
Hospital in Carson Springs
just called CBI.

562
00:32:38,016 --> 00:32:41,978
Someone left a baby girl with a birthmark
on her arm in the waiting room.

563
00:32:42,145 --> 00:32:43,813
Now, if you two want to see her,
you better come with us

564
00:32:43,938 --> 00:32:45,982
'cause they're gonna let you
anywhere near her otherwise.

565
00:32:46,149 --> 00:32:48,818
And if it is Caitlyn,
she's evidence.

566
00:32:48,985 --> 00:32:50,820
- Okay?
- Why would he come?

567
00:32:51,237 --> 00:32:52,280
I'm her father.

568
00:32:52,489 --> 00:32:53,782
- Just...
- And a fine one you are.

569
00:32:53,948 --> 00:32:54,991
- You step back, old man!
- Okay!

570
00:32:55,116 --> 00:32:56,993
- Will you try me?
- If you want what's best for Caitlyn

571
00:32:57,118 --> 00:32:58,620
you need to call a truce.

572
00:32:59,079 --> 00:33:00,622
Let's go.
Which hospital is it?

573
00:33:00,789 --> 00:33:02,957
- There's more than one?
- There's three.

574
00:33:03,958 --> 00:33:07,170
She, uh... she didn't
say which one.

575
00:33:07,629 --> 00:33:10,757
Let's find out what...
Van Pelt?

576
00:33:11,049 --> 00:33:13,635
Oh, damn it! My phone
just ran out of charge.

577
00:33:13,760 --> 00:33:16,054
- Can you call her?
- No. My phone is in the car.

578
00:33:16,221 --> 00:33:18,306
Miriam, can I borrow your phone
just for one second?

579
00:33:18,556 --> 00:33:19,808
Thank you.

580
00:33:26,856 --> 00:33:29,109
- Van Pelt?
- Okay, I'm ready.

581
00:33:29,317 --> 00:33:31,236
Yeah, which hospital is it?

582
00:33:31,444 --> 00:33:33,530
Apparently there are three, which,

583
00:33:33,738 --> 00:33:36,199
"is kind of odd, considering
it's such a small place."

584
00:33:36,324 --> 00:33:38,743
Okay. I'm tracking the last number
she dialed.

585
00:33:42,956 --> 00:33:43,998
Got it.

586
00:33:44,124 --> 00:33:47,168
- St. Vincent's. Thank you.
- What are you looking at?

587
00:33:47,293 --> 00:33:49,129
I'm looking at a big,
tall, dirty peasant.

588
00:33:49,295 --> 00:33:51,381
- What are you looking at?
- You know, I already warned you two.

589
00:33:51,756 --> 00:33:53,383
- A dead man.
- Yeah, I told you...

590
00:33:53,508 --> 00:33:54,592
- Let's go.
- Yeah, let's go.

591
00:33:54,717 --> 00:33:56,511
Um, here. Thank you
for the use of your phone.

592
00:33:57,220 --> 00:33:59,222
- Let's get out of here.
- We'll be in touch. Goodbye.

593
00:34:04,978 --> 00:34:07,814
Listen. I hate to mess
with you, but, uh...

594
00:34:09,232 --> 00:34:12,193
I was lying again.
No Caitlyn.

595
00:34:12,318 --> 00:34:15,071
But we'll have her very soon.
I promise.

596
00:34:15,655 --> 00:34:17,615
And... And...
and we'll be in touch.

597
00:34:17,782 --> 00:34:19,284
Okay?

598
00:34:30,209 --> 00:34:35,173
Thank you, Grace.
15009 Ashley Ridge drive.

599
00:34:35,798 --> 00:34:38,092
- Told you it'd work.
- Hasn't worked yet.

600
00:34:38,342 --> 00:34:40,595
She has to figure out
what we're up to.

601
00:34:40,720 --> 00:34:43,264
At this very moment, she's probably
calling whoever has the baby

602
00:34:43,389 --> 00:34:45,016
and telling them
to get the hell out of there.

603
00:34:45,183 --> 00:34:47,101
How's she gonna warn them?
Her phone's dead.

604
00:34:48,478 --> 00:34:49,896
She could use the landline.

605
00:34:50,021 --> 00:34:51,189
I bet she doesn't know
the number.

606
00:34:51,355 --> 00:34:52,857
I mean, no one knows
numbers these days.

607
00:34:52,982 --> 00:34:54,775
You just have them programmed
into your phone.

608
00:35:26,557 --> 00:35:29,852
Hello.
Uh... yes?

609
00:35:30,686 --> 00:35:31,896
Hi.

610
00:36:04,262 --> 00:36:06,722
- Where's Ruth?
- She's under arrest.

611
00:36:08,599 --> 00:36:10,017
She didn't know what I did.

612
00:36:10,184 --> 00:36:13,646
She thought she was just taking care
of a child in a custody dispute.

613
00:36:13,813 --> 00:36:15,314
So she said.

614
00:36:18,276 --> 00:36:19,443
How did you know?

615
00:36:19,610 --> 00:36:22,196
The diapers and the milk
were taken from the motel room

616
00:36:22,363 --> 00:36:25,241
which told me that Red John's
partner was someone frugal.

617
00:36:25,408 --> 00:36:27,577
Very organized, meticulous.

618
00:36:27,743 --> 00:36:30,204
Someone who would take care
of the baby.

619
00:36:30,371 --> 00:36:33,082
Probably a woman.
Middle age.

620
00:36:34,458 --> 00:36:35,960
Wanting a child.

621
00:36:36,085 --> 00:36:38,004
I told Eileen that Caitlyn
would be taken away

622
00:36:38,170 --> 00:36:42,133
by social services if she didn't completely
separate herself from Roddy.

623
00:36:42,258 --> 00:36:44,677
She was devastated,
but she did it.

624
00:36:44,844 --> 00:36:47,847
She moved to the motel.
Easy pickings.

625
00:36:48,055 --> 00:36:52,018
You did all this for a child?
Have you heard of adoption?

626
00:36:52,143 --> 00:36:55,104
Well, sure. But this way
I could help Red John also.

627
00:36:55,229 --> 00:36:59,317
And Caitlyn's such a lovely girl.
Always happy and smiling.

628
00:36:59,442 --> 00:37:02,069
- Tell me about Red John.
- He's been a good friend to me.

629
00:37:02,194 --> 00:37:05,114
- For how long?
- A long time. A long time.

630
00:37:05,239 --> 00:37:08,200
- Why did he kill Eileen?
- I don't know.

631
00:37:08,367 --> 00:37:11,329
You don't ask him questions.
But it had to be her.

632
00:37:11,454 --> 00:37:14,123
It was important to him
that it was her.

633
00:37:16,584 --> 00:37:19,211
He told me this might happen,
and if it did

634
00:37:19,337 --> 00:37:21,255
that I should give you something.

635
00:37:22,131 --> 00:37:24,258
- Easy.
- It's okay.

636
00:37:24,717 --> 00:37:26,177
I mean you no harm.

637
00:37:41,067 --> 00:37:43,944
- What is it?
- I'm done talking.

638
00:38:26,946 --> 00:38:30,408
"Something's gotten hold
of my heart"

639
00:38:31,033 --> 00:38:35,871
"keeping my soul
and my senses apart"

640
00:38:37,665 --> 00:38:41,961
"Something's gotten
into my life"

641
00:38:42,169 --> 00:38:46,424
"cutting its way through
my dreams like a knife"

642
00:38:47,258 --> 00:38:49,218
"Turning me up"

643
00:38:49,844 --> 00:38:52,012
"and turning me down"

644
00:38:52,638 --> 00:38:55,182
"Making me smile"

645
00:38:55,307 --> 00:38:58,269
"and making me frown"

646
00:39:16,370 --> 00:39:17,788
What's on the disc?

647
00:39:32,511 --> 00:39:34,138
"Hello, Patrick."

648
00:39:34,972 --> 00:39:37,850
"As you can see,
things didn't go as I planned."

649
00:39:38,392 --> 00:39:40,311
"Don't say I told you so."

650
00:39:40,770 --> 00:39:43,564
"Red John wants me
to read a message to you"

651
00:39:44,231 --> 00:39:47,359
"and in return, he won't
make me suffer so much."

652
00:39:48,068 --> 00:39:49,445
"He was really mad at me"

653
00:39:49,612 --> 00:39:54,241
"so I think this is very fair
under the circumstances."

654
00:40:03,292 --> 00:40:04,752
"Patrick"

655
00:40:05,169 --> 00:40:08,589
"Lorelei told me what she told you
about shaking my hand."

656
00:40:09,298 --> 00:40:11,550
"So I know that you've
made a list"

657
00:40:11,759 --> 00:40:14,637
"and I know that by the time
you watch this video"

658
00:40:15,095 --> 00:40:18,140
"you'll have narrowed
that list down to a few names."

659
00:40:18,349 --> 00:40:21,143
"That's quite a feat
of memory and research."

660
00:40:21,310 --> 00:40:22,686
"Bravo."

661
00:40:23,354 --> 00:40:25,523
"I bet you think
you're pretty damn clever"

662
00:40:26,524 --> 00:40:27,817
"but you're not."

663
00:40:28,526 --> 00:40:31,654
"You got a lucky break.
That's not clever."

664
00:40:32,363 --> 00:40:33,906
"I'll show you clever."

665
00:40:34,990 --> 00:40:38,452
"I'm going to kill a happy memory
that you've never told anyone."

666
00:40:39,161 --> 00:40:41,163
"And when you investigate"

667
00:40:41,330 --> 00:40:43,666
"I'm going to lead you
right to this video."

668
00:40:45,501 --> 00:40:47,086
"There's more."

669
00:40:47,503 --> 00:40:49,922
"Right now, I want you
to take out"

670
00:40:50,089 --> 00:40:52,508
"your list of suspects
and look at the names."

671
00:40:53,217 --> 00:40:54,718
"I'll give you a moment."

672
00:40:57,972 --> 00:40:59,181
"Okay."

673
00:40:59,598 --> 00:41:01,058
"The names are..."

674
00:41:01,767 --> 00:41:03,477
"Bret Stiles..."

675
00:41:04,770 --> 00:41:06,105
"Gale Bertram..."

676
00:41:09,817 --> 00:41:11,694
"Raymond Haffner..."

677
00:41:13,362 --> 00:41:14,822
"Reede Smith..."

678
00:41:15,906 --> 00:41:17,283
"Bob Kirkland..."

679
00:41:19,535 --> 00:41:21,871
"Sheriff Thomas McAllister..."

680
00:41:23,539 --> 00:41:24,957
"Brett Partridge."

681
00:41:25,708 --> 00:41:29,253
"There. See?
That's clever."

682
00:41:30,296 --> 00:41:32,381
"But fair's fair, Patrick."

683
00:41:32,548 --> 00:41:35,593
"You've changed the game,
so there's new rules now."

684
00:41:36,552 --> 00:41:39,138
"Eileen Turner
is the first of many."

685
00:41:40,097 --> 00:41:43,183
"I'm going to start
killing again. Often."

686
00:41:43,684 --> 00:41:45,436
"Until you catch me..."

687
00:41:47,563 --> 00:41:49,565
"or I catch you."

